**Conclusion:** all 40,000 rays match brute force exactly on triangle index and `t`; the shared-edge, inside-root, outlier, and degenerate cases pass; build time is 0.2–36 ms; traversal runs 2.7k–12.9k rays/s with 16.9–19.4 node visits/ray; and ordered traversal visits strictly fewer nodes than the same tree traversed unordered (9.3% aggregate reduction, and strictly fewer in every scene).
